join durai left
join oleysa right

durai: HEY EVERYBODY! COME INSIDE FOR GREAT DEALS!
durai: I SEE YOU TRYING TO IGNORE ME, MA'AM! COME IN FOR SOME GREAT DEALS!
durai: HEY LITTLE GUY! DO YOU LIKE GREAT SAVINGS ON HOUSEHOLD ITEMS? I SURE DO! NYUK NYUK NYUK!
oleysa: Ugh.
Durai enters
durai: "Do you like... great savings", eh... "Do you like, deep discounts", I don't know...
durai: Hey, Oley!
oleysa: Hm. No Oley works here, I'm afraid. No idea who you mean.
durai: Oleysa, radiant as ever.
durai: Listen. I have a question about the character you gave me to play. Not totally sure which way it should go, thought it'd be best to bring it up with you.
oleysa: Breadsworth is very simple. He was born to promote this store and if he ever stops doing that, then he will die.
oleysa: He has come to terms with this situation and is always smiling and happy. He always tries his hardest to get customers inside.
durai: Yeah, yeah yeah yeah. I know. But like, would the character say "great savings" or "deep discounts"? I can't really decide.
oleysa: Breadsworth would not worry about this. He'd just go outside and make loud noises to get people's attention.
durai: Look, heh... that's not really how the game is played.
durai: The way I do it, with the stakes, and the drama, it might not get people into the store, but it touches their hearts.
durai: This is the essence of acting. I feel like you don't quite understand.
oleysa: Durai...
oleysa: Do you know how much it costs to run an inflatable tube man for one hour?
durai: A... what?
oleysa: You know what I mean. Those big wavy guys outside carwashes. 
oleysa: It costs £40 to fill those with enough hot air for an hour.
oleysa: Do you know how much we pay you per hour?
durai: £23.19.
oleysa: See, that's why we have you out there. Not to touch people's hearts.
durai: ...
durai: You... will never understand me.
Durai leaves
durai: HEY EVERYBODY! HEAR ABOUT THE STORY OF THE ARTIST WHO FELL INTO HIS OWN CREATION!
durai: LEGEND SAYS IF YOU BUY MY BREAD, HE MIGHT GET OUT!
durai: I SEE YOU TRYING TO IGNORE ME! PLEASE, I REALLY NEED YOU TO JUST COME IN.
oleysa: Oh, Durai... you poor boy.
game: Oleysa seems to have really hurt Durai - he couldn't get people to buy stuff as much as usual. Bad shift.
[signal arg="shift_bad"]